From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meerzulee <17146298+meerzulee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:10:25 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: icc: use strscpy_pad() for the adapter name

Linux 7.2 removed strncpy(). strscpy_pad() writes the same bytes for
this short constant name: the string, a terminating NUL and zero
padding to the end of the buffer.
---
 drivers/ps4/icc/i2c.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ps4/icc/i2c.c b/drivers/ps4/icc/i2c.c
index 7317a6985e3657bb124bb4053ccb609fc0f5e473..4b8e71736ac65198443859049ef7b55394a28700 100644
--- a/drivers/ps4/icc/i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/ps4/icc/i2c.c
@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ int icc_i2c_init(struct apcie_dev *sc)
 	i2c->algo = &icc_i2c_algo;
 	i2c->algo_data = NULL;
 	i2c->dev.parent = &sc->pdev->dev;
-	strncpy(i2c->name, "icc", sizeof(i2c->name));
+	strscpy_pad(i2c->name, "icc");
 	i2c_set_adapdata(i2c, sc);
 	ret = i2c_add_adapter(i2c);
 	if (ret < 0) {
